🐒🐊 The Monkey and the Crocodile

Once upon a time, a clever monkey lived on a fruit tree by a river. The tree was full of sweet, juicy fruits.

One day, a crocodile came swimming by. The monkey greeted him kindly and offered him some fruits. The crocodile happily accepted, and soon they became good friends.

Every day, the monkey gave the crocodile fresh fruits to eat.

One day, the crocodile took some fruits home for his wife. She loved the taste and said, “If the fruits are so sweet, the monkey’s heart must be even sweeter! Bring me the monkey’s heart.”

The crocodile was shocked. “But he is my friend,” he said. Still, he sadly agreed.

The next day, the crocodile went to the monkey and said, “My friend, come visit my home.”

The monkey trusted him and climbed onto his back. As they swam across the river, the crocodile felt uneasy. Finally, he told the truth.

“My wife wants to eat your heart,” he said.

The monkey was frightened, but he stayed calm. He quickly thought of a clever plan.

“Oh dear!” said the monkey. “I left my heart on the tree. Let’s go back and get it.”

The foolish crocodile believed him and turned back toward the tree.

As soon as they reached the riverbank, the monkey quickly jumped onto the tree.

“You silly crocodile!” he said. “Who leaves their heart behind? You tried to trick me, but I was smarter.”

The crocodile felt ashamed and swam away.

The monkey stayed safe and never trusted the crocodile again.

💖 Moral:

Think wisely in difficult situations to solve problems.
